// THE AMULET OF ETERNAL GLORY - a glory whose charge counter is gone. Four teleports, forever.
//
// It is entirely ~glory_teleport_to, which amulet_of_glory.rs2 factored out as a proc for the
// mounted glory in a quest hall - a glory with nothing to charge, which is exactly what this is.
// So the whole of this file is "the glory's teleport, and do not spend anything".
//
// NOT category_557. That category is the four CHARGED amulets and its wearop handlers decrement
// (amulet_of_glory.rs2's ~amulet_of_glory_worn calls ~worn_replace with next_obj_stage). This one
// carries its own category so that it cannot pick those up by accident - the one bug that would
// matter here is an eternal amulet that quietly turns into a glory(3).
//
// Where it comes from: area_wilderness/scripts/fountain_of_rune.rs2, 1 in 250 per recharge.

[opheld4,_amulet_of_eternal_glory]
// No charge message, because there is no charge. The glory's own line here would be "Your amulet
// has three charges left."
~glory_teleport("The amulet's light does not dim.");

[label,wearop1__amulet_of_eternal_glory] ~glory_teleport_to(1, "The amulet's light does not dim.");
[label,wearop2__amulet_of_eternal_glory] ~glory_teleport_to(2, "The amulet's light does not dim.");
[label,wearop3__amulet_of_eternal_glory] ~glory_teleport_to(3, "The amulet's light does not dim.");
[label,wearop4__amulet_of_eternal_glory] ~glory_teleport_to(4, "The amulet's light does not dim.");
